   "id": "gb-strata-florida",
   "name": "Strata Florida",
   "region": "gb-wales",
   "summary": "The best-known green lane in Britain, and the one people travel for. An old drovers' road over the Cambrian Mountains from the abbey ruins at Pontrhydfendigaid, with a string of river crossings that turn it from a ride into an event after rain.",
   "days": 1,
   "warning": "The river crossings are the whole point and also the danger. They rise fast and the bed moves; what was ankle deep in the morning is not in the afternoon.",
