   "name": "Salisbury Plain",
   "region": "gb-south-west",
   "summary": "Hundreds of miles of legal byway over open chalk downland, and the biggest concentration of green lane in southern England. Fast, grassy and wide, with the abandoned village of Imber and the military ranges in the middle of it.",
