  {
   "id": "gb-ridgeway",
   "name": "The Ridgeway byways",
   "region": "gb-south-east",
   "summary": "Britain's oldest road, and the byway sections of it are still open to vehicles. Chalk track along the crest of the downs past Avebury and Barbury Castle, with views over half of Wiltshire and nothing modern in sight.",
   "days": 1,
   "warning": "Only parts of the Ridgeway are byway - the rest is bridleway and footpath, and the boundary is not obvious on the ground. Voluntary winter restraint is widely observed.",
